  "details": "I have had this bug for a few months, but in the last week it has become unbearable to play this way. Until the second half of 2020 I played vrchat normally until I started to have the screen frozen randomly (for no reason) even though I was alone on the map. My game crashes a little and when I come back I still listen to the people around me, according to friends I keep moving, however my headset display is frozen (in a 1 second loop of what I was seeing at the time of the crash), if i look at the desktop, my vrchat is totally frozen. I find it strange that regardless of the game I play vrchat is the only thing that occurs to me with my vr headset. I wanted some feedback if it has any resolution (I've done everything from lowering the resolution in steam vr to formatting the computer) and I believe it is not my computer because when this bug started I had several friends with the same problems but after some game patches returned to work normally for them... If necessary ask that I post some log of a crash moment.",
